# tls_server.dict - what the server engine compares a client's octets against (libFuzzer cannot
# see it in NASM code): the record headers of each type at 0x0303, a change_cipher_spec record
# whole, alert records (close_notify, user_canceled, a fatal one), the handshake types a client
# sends (ClientHello, Finished, KeyUpdate and its two values), the extension types a ClientHello
# carries that the server reads, supported_versions' lists (TLS 1.3, and 1.2 alone), the groups
# (every NamedGroup the engine has, and one it lacks), the suites, the signature schemes, and
# record_size_limit's floor.
